Morning, larry.

252
00:14:44,951 --> 00:14:47,587
The time is 6:4.

253
00:14:49,789 --> 00:14:52,525
Delayed puberty awareness
programs, here.

254
00:14:57,864 --> 00:15:01,601
Man, there’s an amazing number
of csonkas.

255
00:15:06,172 --> 00:15:09,475
[Grunts]

256
00:15:09,475 --> 00:15:10,676
So we’re just
watching someone

257
00:15:10,676 --> 00:15:12,245
fritter away
their afternoon here.

258
00:15:12,245 --> 00:15:14,147
Mm-hm.

259
00:15:14,147 --> 00:15:16,849
- Operator.
- Hi, could I have
information, please?

260
00:15:16,849 --> 00:15:18,518
One moment, please.

261
00:15:18,518 --> 00:15:22,288
Now, that’s two moments.
I’m sorry.

262
00:15:22,288 --> 00:15:23,656
Information.

263
00:15:23,656 --> 00:15:25,525
Hi, could I have the number
for mike pipper?

264
00:15:25,525 --> 00:15:26,592
No.

265
00:15:26,592 --> 00:15:28,895
P-i-p-p-e-r.

266
00:15:28,895 --> 00:15:30,830
For what city, please?

267
00:15:30,830 --> 00:15:34,200
- From eaglehat.
- One moment.

268
00:15:34,200 --> 00:15:37,170
Eaglehat?

269
00:15:37,170 --> 00:15:39,605
I’ sorry, there’s no listing
for an m. Pipper.

270
00:15:39,605 --> 00:15:41,007
Oh, okay, thanks.

271
00:15:41,007 --> 00:15:45,511
And the investigation
comes to a close.

272
00:15:45,511 --> 00:15:48,781
Well, I better get to reading
my x-men comics.

273
00:15:52,518 --> 00:15:57,023
Hey, get this caterpillar
off my lip.

274
00:15:57,023 --> 00:15:59,759
Well, larry,
I guess I better get going.

275
00:15:59,759 --> 00:16:03,262
Say hello
to jim kiick for me.

276
00:16:04,630 --> 00:16:06,933
[Door knocks]

277
00:16:06,933 --> 00:16:10,203
Come in.

278
00:16:10,203 --> 00:16:13,472
Mrs. Costanza!

279
00:16:13,472 --> 00:16:15,708
There. What are you studying?

280
00:16:15,708 --> 00:16:17,143
French revolution.

281
00:16:17,143 --> 00:16:19,779
Oh, that looks more like
world war ii.

282
00:16:19,779 --> 00:16:21,614
[Chuckles]
Oh, i’m a caution.

283
00:16:21,614 --> 00:16:23,816
Where did you get that?

284
00:16:23,816 --> 00:16:25,351
I found it in the attic.

285
00:16:25,351 --> 00:16:28,287
Leave me alone, mom.
I’m starting a software company.

286
00:16:28,287 --> 00:16:29,856
Well, don’t work too late.

287
00:16:29,856 --> 00:16:31,724
I’ll lock you in as usual.

288
00:16:31,724 --> 00:16:34,026
What was he like?

289
00:16:34,026 --> 00:16:37,063
Now, troy, we’ve talked
about this before.

290
00:16:37,063 --> 00:16:39,165
I don’t want you to cry
about what is passed.

291
00:16:39,165 --> 00:16:42,001
No emotions.
We’ve discussed that.

292
00:16:42,001 --> 00:16:43,870
Is that why you locked up
his stuff in the attic?

293
00:16:43,870 --> 00:16:45,771
You didn’t want me
to get upset?

294
00:16:45,771 --> 00:16:48,040
You found that--?

295
00:16:48,040 --> 00:16:51,177
Troy, you had
no business there.

296
00:16:51,177 --> 00:16:54,480
My father is my business.

297
00:16:54,480 --> 00:16:57,917
Al louis as grandma.

298
00:16:57,917 --> 00:17:01,354
Oh, troy, i’m sorry.

299
00:17:01,354 --> 00:17:03,789
I only want you
to forget him.

300
00:17:03,789 --> 00:17:05,358
Carry on with your own life.

301
00:17:05,358 --> 00:17:07,326
Yeah, once you get one.

302
00:17:12,465 --> 00:17:13,766
Am I like him?

303
00:17:13,766 --> 00:17:17,303
No, he was masculine
and likable.

304
00:17:17,303 --> 00:17:19,171
Yes.

305
00:17:19,171 --> 00:17:20,840
You’re very much like him.

306
00:17:20,840 --> 00:17:23,509
If i’m thinking
of the right guy.

307
00:17:26,178 --> 00:17:29,949
Man, now my room stinks
of youth dew.

308
00:17:32,351 --> 00:17:37,156
Mvp, super bowl viii
for miami.

309
00:17:37,156 --> 00:17:39,258
Seven years later.

310
00:17:40,459 --> 00:17:42,962
[Car engine failing]

311
00:17:42,962 --> 00:17:45,464
That’s enough trees
for the spotted owl, isn’t it?

312
00:17:45,464 --> 00:17:46,933
Sure.

313
00:17:49,735 --> 00:17:52,371
Uh-oh, the town’s alternator
is shot.

314
00:17:56,509 --> 00:17:59,645
Free pictures of brian mulroney
with fill up.

315
00:18:04,383 --> 00:18:07,453
Oh, and who says there aren’t
any nice homes in canada?

316
00:18:15,761 --> 00:18:18,531
Check it out.

317
00:18:18,531 --> 00:18:22,902
Someone’s scratching
his belly.

318
00:18:22,902 --> 00:18:24,770
Damn!

319
00:18:24,770 --> 00:18:28,407
When it’s above 50 or below 40
it never starts.

320
00:18:33,813 --> 00:18:37,249
Canada is for lovers.

321
00:18:39,852 --> 00:18:40,886
His truck won’t start,

322
00:18:40,886 --> 00:18:43,489
but at least
his tablecloth is dry.

323
00:18:47,360 --> 00:18:50,629
If you lived here,
you’d be in hell by now.

324
00:18:52,298 --> 00:18:54,467
Check out
the linc hayes topiary.

325
00:18:54,467 --> 00:18:57,837
Cool.

326
00:18:57,837 --> 00:18:59,939
[Humming]

327
00:18:59,939 --> 00:19:02,641
Hitchcock’s parade of homes.

328
00:19:06,278 --> 00:19:10,616
Aw, it’s
the came-with-the-frame family.

329
00:19:10,616 --> 00:19:12,551
Water me!

330
00:19:12,551 --> 00:19:17,089
[Coughing]

331
00:19:17,089 --> 00:19:20,292
Hey, another kid
exactly like him across town.

332
00:19:22,828 --> 00:19:24,430
He just finished
his exhaustive

333
00:19:24,430 --> 00:19:27,133
four-volume biography
of larry csonka.

334
00:19:27,133 --> 00:19:30,002
[Clock chimes]

335
00:19:30,002 --> 00:19:33,906
Someone’s hitting a fry pan,
which means it’s 8:00.

336
00:19:35,841 --> 00:19:38,611
Of course the clock’s set
to miami time.

337
00:19:42,281 --> 00:19:45,818
Well, swing choir ain’t gonna
rehearse itself.

338
00:19:49,955 --> 00:19:51,657
Called in
for the night shift.

339
00:19:51,657 --> 00:19:55,194
Apparently auntie never
got laid-off after the war.

340
00:20:01,067 --> 00:20:03,736
Why did he put a laserdisc
in the refrigerator.

341
00:20:05,971 --> 00:20:07,606
Hey, el santo!

342
00:20:07,606 --> 00:20:08,874
Hey!

343
00:20:12,411 --> 00:20:16,048
Ah, let’s see if there’s any
larry csonka movies on tonight.

344
00:20:22,021 --> 00:20:23,956
Can I discipline you?

345
00:20:28,160 --> 00:20:29,795
[Chewing sounds]

346
00:20:29,795 --> 00:20:33,299
Cold crazy bread. Mm.
Really is crazy.

347
00:20:36,135 --> 00:20:40,239
Wait, I haven’t read tolkien
in almost a week.

348
00:20:42,208 --> 00:20:46,178
Script is punched up
by harpo marx.

349
00:20:46,178 --> 00:20:49,348
Ah, a yanni song
is about to begin.

350
00:20:54,954 --> 00:20:58,057
What would
coach don shula do?

351
00:21:05,097 --> 00:21:06,599
[Grunting sounds]

352
00:21:06,599 --> 00:21:09,768
It’s his michael feinstein
signature bat.

353
00:21:12,972 --> 00:21:16,775
Tee-hee, tee-hee.

354
00:21:16,775 --> 00:21:20,679
His head is still
factory wrapped.

355
00:21:20,679 --> 00:21:23,916
Is he a door-to-door
executioner?

356
00:21:37,763 --> 00:21:40,666
Ow! I was just going to
read the meter.

357
00:21:46,071 --> 00:21:47,940
You know it’s spring
when the executioners

358
00:21:47,940 --> 00:21:49,842
start getting in the house.

359
00:21:53,979 --> 00:21:57,216
It’s open. Please.

360
00:22:02,388 --> 00:22:04,957
THE McCULLOCHS ARE HERE.

361
00:22:13,132 --> 00:22:16,202
Can I interest you
in a replacement door?

362
00:22:22,074 --> 00:22:26,478
Canadian villain,
garth vader.

363
00:22:26,478 --> 00:22:29,281
Icky flakes. Ugh.

364
00:22:30,849 --> 00:22:33,586
Ah, that was
a good seven years.

365
00:22:36,121 --> 00:22:40,259
Troy! I know
you can hear me, troy.

366
00:22:40,259 --> 00:22:42,995
I know you have the map.

367
00:22:42,995 --> 00:22:44,296
I want it.

368
00:22:44,296 --> 00:22:46,999
Jesse "the body" ventura
dubbed his voice.

369
00:22:51,337 --> 00:22:54,039
Wow, auntie sent
her jack-booted thugs

370
00:22:54,039 --> 00:22:56,575
to make him lunch.

371
00:23:03,382 --> 00:23:07,119
We just want to cut
your sugar-cane crop.

372
00:23:12,258 --> 00:23:15,294
You thugs, don’t run
with your scimitars.

373
00:23:16,795 --> 00:23:20,799
Dam, he’s got a 10-speed.

374
00:23:20,799 --> 00:23:24,536
Get on the banana-seat bike,
and give chase.

375
00:23:24,536 --> 00:23:25,804
Let’s get out of here.

376
00:23:25,804 --> 00:23:29,241
Hey man, thank your sister
for sewing our hoods.

377
00:23:40,352 --> 00:23:41,887
[Laughter]

378
00:23:41,887 --> 00:23:44,923
And then the drunk guy says,
I can’t help being an idiot,

379
00:23:44,923 --> 00:23:46,325
i’m canadian.

380
00:23:46,325 --> 00:23:47,927
[Laughter]

381
00:23:47,927 --> 00:23:50,496
You’re right,
they’re so pathetic, mike.

382
00:23:50,496 --> 00:23:51,864
[Whistle blows]

383
00:23:51,864 --> 00:23:53,365
Huh?

384
00:23:53,365 --> 00:23:56,936
Enough! There’s been too much
canada bashing for far too long.

385
00:23:56,936 --> 00:23:58,971
I say no more.

386
00:23:58,971 --> 00:24:01,073
Don’t you mean, no more eh?

387
00:24:01,073 --> 00:24:02,374
- [Laugher]
- Good one, man.

388
00:24:02,374 --> 00:24:04,076
They are so stupid.

389
00:24:04,076 --> 00:24:05,277
Stop it now.

390
00:24:05,277 --> 00:24:07,079
Instead let us offer
our northern brothers

391
00:24:07,079 --> 00:24:10,115
and sisters
this song of tribute.

392
00:24:10,115 --> 00:24:14,253
♪ Oh, I wish I was back
in old canada ♪

393
00:24:14,253 --> 00:24:17,456
♪ a land which I never
shall lampoon ♪

394
00:24:17,456 --> 00:24:21,060
♪ how I pine for the ice
covering lake manitoba ♪

395
00:24:21,060 --> 00:24:24,063
♪ and the beauty
that is saskatoon ♪

396
00:24:24,063 --> 00:24:25,397
I got one.

397
00:24:25,397 --> 00:24:28,133
♪ I wish I was stuck
in the hills of alberta ♪

398
00:24:28,133 --> 00:24:31,637
♪ drinking beer with some
big, dumb guy trapping fur ♪

399
00:24:31,637 --> 00:24:33,272
♪ as he scraped
and he chiseled ♪

400
00:24:33,272 --> 00:24:35,140
♪ all the moose dung
off his boots ♪

401
00:24:35,140 --> 00:24:37,609
♪ I would learn
that he’s the prime minister ♪

402
00:24:37,609 --> 00:24:39,178
Oh, stop that.

403
00:24:39,178 --> 00:24:42,681
♪ Oh, I wish I was in the land
that gave us peter jennings ♪

404
00:24:42,681 --> 00:24:45,651
♪ alanis morissette,
mike myers too ♪

405
00:24:45,651 --> 00:24:47,920
♪ no, I take that back
I wouldn’t go there ♪

406
00:24:47,920 --> 00:24:49,421
♪ even in you paid me ♪

407
00:24:49,421 --> 00:24:52,024
♪ oh, canada, you are a place
I must eschew ♪

408
00:24:52,024 --> 00:24:53,892
Now this is not in the spirit
that I intended.

409
00:24:53,892 --> 00:24:55,361
Oh, come on. Give in.

410
00:24:55,361 --> 00:24:58,530
I mean, after all, they gave us
ed the sock and rush.

411
00:24:58,530 --> 00:25:00,599
Yeah, what are you defending?
They’re such feebs.

412
00:25:00,599 --> 00:25:03,202
- Okay, i’ll try.
- All right. Good man.

413
00:25:03,202 --> 00:25:07,339
♪ Oh, I wish I was blowing up
prince edward island ♪

414
00:25:07,339 --> 00:25:10,409
♪ going on to bomb ontario ♪

415
00:25:10,409 --> 00:25:13,879
♪ the destruction of canada
and all of its culture ♪

416
00:25:13,879 --> 00:25:16,849
♪ is by far
my favorite scenario ♪

417
00:25:16,849 --> 00:25:18,584
Okay, that’s a little strong.
You might want to back it down.

418
00:25:18,584 --> 00:25:20,886
No, no you were right, mike.
This is much more fun.

419
00:25:20,886 --> 00:25:22,488
♪ Just where the hell does
canada get off ♪

420
00:25:22,488 --> 00:25:24,757
♪ sharing a border ♪

421
00:25:24,757 --> 00:25:27,092
♪ with countries
far superior to it? ♪

422
00:25:27,092 --> 00:25:28,360
Yikes.

423
00:25:28,360 --> 00:25:30,295
♪ Why you lousy, stinkin’,
francophonic, ♪

424
00:25:30,295 --> 00:25:31,930
♪ bacon loving bastards ♪

425
00:25:31,930 --> 00:25:33,966
♪ your country’s
just a giant piece of-- ♪

426
00:25:33,966 --> 00:25:35,267
- Whoa, whoa, whoa, easy!
- Okay, I think that’s enough.

427
00:25:35,267 --> 00:25:37,469
I think we going to cambot.
Okay, thanks.

428
00:25:37,469 --> 00:25:38,570
- All right.
- Wow.

429
00:25:38,570 --> 00:25:40,305
I have no
sense of proportion.

430
00:25:40,305 --> 00:25:42,474
I’m a disgrace to my uniform.

431
00:25:42,474 --> 00:25:44,343
No, that’s okay.
Now, calm down.

432
00:25:44,343 --> 00:25:45,978
Now, we mustn’t hate.
Mustn’t hate.

433
00:25:45,978 --> 00:25:47,479
At least so overtly.

434
00:25:47,479 --> 00:25:50,182
Exactly right. Must disguise
our hate just a little.

435
00:25:50,182 --> 00:25:52,651
We’ll be right back.
Ssh, ssh, it’s okay now, dudley.

436
00:25:52,651 --> 00:25:54,653
- Calm down. Calm down.
- Pardonnez-moi.

437
00:25:54,653 --> 00:25:56,355
Pardonnez-moi.

438
00:25:56,355 --> 00:25:58,290
♪♪

439
00:26:05,330 --> 00:26:08,567
Seven years later.

440
00:26:08,567 --> 00:26:10,969
Dental hygienist of the week.

441
00:26:16,375 --> 00:26:17,743
Yeah, once he gets it started,

442
00:26:17,743 --> 00:26:19,378
he’s going to drive it
to the front yard,

443
00:26:19,378 --> 00:26:21,313
take a couple of tires off,
and let it rust

444
00:26:21,313 --> 00:26:25,584
next to the old freezer
sitting on the front lawn.

445
00:26:25,584 --> 00:26:27,586
Ah.

446
00:26:27,586 --> 00:26:29,621
In my work
for a bloodthirsty cult,

447
00:26:29,621 --> 00:26:32,224
I depend on my gran torino.

448
00:26:32,224 --> 00:26:36,395
I think his menace is undercut
by the "baby on board" tag.

449
00:26:39,731 --> 00:26:43,836
Hey, I think your cameraman’s
stuck in the door.

450
00:26:43,836 --> 00:26:45,971
See?

451
00:26:49,107 --> 00:26:51,777
CAN YOU IMAGINE HOW MANY
POTATO OLé CONTAINERS

452
00:26:51,777 --> 00:26:54,480
are on the floor of that car?

453
00:26:56,215 --> 00:26:59,818
This music is really more suited
to plate spinning.

454
00:26:59,818 --> 00:27:02,120
Kind of a mazurka.

455
00:27:04,823 --> 00:27:08,293
I’m losing track
of the crappy vehicles here.

456
00:27:11,964 --> 00:27:15,567
Crank the molly hatchet
and let’s roll!

457
00:27:15,567 --> 00:27:16,902
[Radio chatter]

458
00:27:16,902 --> 00:27:20,405
I’m sherry.

459
00:27:20,405 --> 00:27:22,474
This is carol dolan,
and i’ll be back.

460
00:27:22,474 --> 00:27:27,045
Aw, now I have to
listen to as it happens.

461
00:27:27,045 --> 00:27:29,748
Honk! Honk! On your ass!

462
00:27:31,917 --> 00:27:35,487
Oh, I love trash--
ow, oh, god.

463
00:27:38,190 --> 00:27:40,425
Maybe it’s the cheap
canadian gas they’re using.

464
00:27:40,425 --> 00:27:43,161
Just can’t get up any speed.

465
00:27:48,967 --> 00:27:51,503
Damn you, peewee!

466
00:27:55,040 --> 00:27:58,443
Hi, i’m billy the building.
[Laughs]

467
00:28:04,650 --> 00:28:06,752
Unfortunately,
the truck’s making a delivery

468
00:28:06,752 --> 00:28:09,221
right back to the cult.

469
00:28:13,659 --> 00:28:15,227
Well, let’s just
go get some bullwhips

470
00:28:15,227 --> 00:28:17,396
and pose for mapplethorpe.

471
00:28:17,396 --> 00:28:19,031
Yup.

472
00:28:22,534 --> 00:28:23,969
Huddled in a pile
of dirty laundry,

473
00:28:23,969 --> 00:28:26,271
it’s just like home.

474
00:28:32,844 --> 00:28:35,914
It sounds like
video-poker music.

475
00:28:40,118 --> 00:28:41,386
And they take refuge

476
00:28:41,386 --> 00:28:43,322
in the anne murray
national forest.

477
00:28:43,322 --> 00:28:45,724
Beautiful, isn’t it?

478
00:28:45,724 --> 00:28:48,327
I think he’s
the tin drum kid.

479
00:28:53,899 --> 00:28:56,802
He’s the kind of clown
who puts $1.87 of gas

480
00:28:56,802 --> 00:28:59,304
in his truck.

481
00:28:59,304 --> 00:29:01,940
Help me, oh,
saint larry csonka.

482
00:29:05,577 --> 00:29:08,647
Well, it went further
than it usually does.

483
00:29:08,647 --> 00:29:11,383
Like a... [coughs]
Rock.

484
00:29:15,287 --> 00:29:18,390
Another human being.
Oh, i’m in for a beating.

485
00:29:24,696 --> 00:29:25,998
What the hell?

486
00:29:25,998 --> 00:29:28,700
I’ve always been
back here, remember?

487
00:29:28,700 --> 00:29:30,836
What are you doing
back there, kid?

488
00:29:30,836 --> 00:29:31,870
I...

489
00:29:31,870 --> 00:29:33,972
I’m laundry.

490
00:29:33,972 --> 00:29:35,140
I needed a ride.

491
00:29:35,140 --> 00:29:37,442
Is he a makeupless clown?

492
00:29:37,442 --> 00:29:38,477
Why don’t you get in the cab?

493
00:29:38,477 --> 00:29:39,578
It’s much
more comfortable there.

494
00:29:39,578 --> 00:29:42,447
Actually, I bet it isn’t.

495
00:29:50,155 --> 00:29:52,557
So, uh, eh then, eh?

496
00:29:52,557 --> 00:29:53,659
[Coughing]

497
00:29:53,659 --> 00:29:56,862
Eh.

498
00:29:56,862 --> 00:29:59,297
Don’t you love
our healthcare system?

499
00:29:59,297 --> 00:30:01,099
Here, put this on.

500
00:30:01,099 --> 00:30:03,669
- It’s made of lunch meat.
- Thanks.

501
00:30:10,208 --> 00:30:12,277
Know anything about motors?

502
00:30:12,277 --> 00:30:15,080
No, sir. Not really.

503
00:30:15,080 --> 00:30:17,849
I know all the songs from
once upon a mattress though.

504
00:30:17,849 --> 00:30:19,618
Let’s have a look.

505
00:30:19,618 --> 00:30:21,353
Are you gonna be a mountie
or a fishing guide

506
00:30:21,353 --> 00:30:23,689
when you grow up?

507
00:30:23,689 --> 00:30:26,391
- Where are you heading?
- Liquor store.

508
00:30:26,391 --> 00:30:29,227
Looks like
i’m heading nowhere.

509
00:30:29,227 --> 00:30:33,231
I see the problem.
The gas line’s loose.

510
00:30:33,231 --> 00:30:34,466
You’re getting behind
the steering wheel,

511
00:30:34,466 --> 00:30:35,867
and crank her over
when I tell you.

512
00:30:35,867 --> 00:30:38,670
He’s wearing fashions
by mac davis.

513
00:30:43,141 --> 00:30:47,112
I’ll just, uh,
pour my garbage in here.

514
00:30:47,112 --> 00:30:48,880
Now!

515
00:30:48,880 --> 00:30:51,083
Kaboom!

516
00:30:51,083 --> 00:30:53,752
Didn’t barbara mandrell
have hair like his at one point?

517
00:30:53,752 --> 00:30:55,454
I think so. Yup, yup.

518
00:30:55,454 --> 00:30:58,757
Put the pedal
all the way down.

519
00:30:58,757 --> 00:31:01,093
Hm, dare I?

520
00:31:01,093 --> 00:31:03,395
[Engine struggling]

521
00:31:06,965 --> 00:31:11,403
Better check this oil here.
Yep, 10w-30.

522
00:31:11,403 --> 00:31:12,604
[Sizzling]

523
00:31:12,604 --> 00:31:15,974
Ooh, his hair’s on fire.

524
00:31:15,974 --> 00:31:17,943
Keep her going, kid!

525
00:31:20,612 --> 00:31:22,848
Okay, bring the brats out.

526
00:31:25,584 --> 00:31:26,718
[Laughs]

527
00:31:26,718 --> 00:31:29,421
Outwitted my truck again!

528
00:31:33,125 --> 00:31:35,327
- WHAT’S YOUR NAME, LADDIE?
- TROY McGREGGOR.

529
00:31:35,327 --> 00:31:37,462
I’m rowsdower.

530
00:31:37,462 --> 00:31:38,730
Zap rowsdower.

531
00:31:38,730 --> 00:31:42,367
Well, my name
is bill shtinkwater.

532
00:31:42,367 --> 00:31:44,770
Rowsdower-mobile away!

533
00:31:44,770 --> 00:31:48,940
And together they fought crime
throughout southwestern alberta!

534
00:31:51,810 --> 00:31:56,715
So, rowsdower,
is that a stupid name, or...?

535
00:31:56,715 --> 00:32:00,952
- Uh, fill her up.
- Yup.

536
00:32:00,952 --> 00:32:03,088
You stay here and i’ll get you
a chocolate bar, okay?

537
00:32:03,088 --> 00:32:04,823
- Thanks.
- Buy me anything in there

538
00:32:04,823 --> 00:32:07,626
with larry csonka on it.
I’ll pay for it.

539
00:32:13,799 --> 00:32:16,768
Shoot, i’m in canada.

540
00:32:24,075 --> 00:32:25,343
Operator, give me the police.

541
00:32:25,343 --> 00:32:28,713
And the cops pick up
their zap rowsdower hotline.

542
00:32:31,449 --> 00:32:33,552
Yes, office, I found this kid
in the back of my truck.

543
00:32:33,552 --> 00:32:37,889
And play in the front seat.

544
00:32:37,889 --> 00:32:40,992
♪ Roll on, big mama,
the highway ♪

545
00:32:40,992 --> 00:32:42,727
How should I know? Ask him.

546
00:32:42,727 --> 00:32:44,796
Ew, gotta get
this dead woodchuck out

547
00:32:44,796 --> 00:32:46,865
from under the seat.
Ew, pooey.

548
00:32:46,865 --> 00:32:49,100
Look, you’re going to
send someone to pick him up?

549
00:32:52,304 --> 00:32:54,306
What do they think
they’re in idaho?

550
00:32:57,142 --> 00:33:01,446
Hey, i’ve got 89 cents
worth of cans back there!

551
00:33:01,446 --> 00:33:04,249
Zap actions-dower.

552
00:33:07,953 --> 00:33:09,087
[Gunshots]

553
00:33:09,087 --> 00:33:12,324
My hood wicks moisture
from my face.

554
00:33:16,795 --> 00:33:21,333
Um, eat my dust.
I don’t know.

555
00:33:21,333 --> 00:33:24,236
Do these pants
go with this sweater?

556
00:33:29,507 --> 00:33:32,811
You know, he blends in.
He looks like a sack of garbage.

557
00:33:32,811 --> 00:33:37,148
Mm-hm.

558
00:33:37,148 --> 00:33:39,684
[Grunts]

559
00:33:42,687 --> 00:33:46,558
This is no time for zymurgy.

560
00:33:46,558 --> 00:33:50,128
Hey, just don’t shoot at me
for a couple of minutes, okay?
Thanks.

561
00:33:54,933 --> 00:33:58,203
If this doesn’t work,
i’ll throw balls of carp dough.

562
00:34:04,809 --> 00:34:07,846
You want us
to pick that up for you?

563
00:34:12,817 --> 00:34:15,787
I knew there was an upside
to being an alcoholic.

564
00:34:17,589 --> 00:34:20,492
Can you take those
to recycling? Thanks.

565
00:34:24,963 --> 00:34:27,332
Canadian mannix!

566
00:34:30,201 --> 00:34:33,939
Uh, so, you wanna
hit the brakes, there, or not?

567
00:34:38,944 --> 00:34:40,845
Oh, i’m so relaxed right now.

568
00:34:40,845 --> 00:34:42,781
♪♪

569
00:34:48,019 --> 00:34:50,422
Rowsdower, I can explain.

570
00:34:50,422 --> 00:34:52,190
Those men
were trying to kill me.

571
00:34:52,190 --> 00:34:55,193
Yeah, tell it
to my acid-washed jeans.

572
00:34:58,229 --> 00:35:00,365
Do you have any idea
what kind of people
you’re dealing with?

573
00:35:00,365 --> 00:35:02,233
They’re from saskatchewan.

574
00:35:02,233 --> 00:35:04,402
No.

575
00:35:04,402 --> 00:35:07,172
- It’s a cult.
- They worship blue oysters.

576
00:35:07,172 --> 00:35:09,407
They want to rule the world.

577
00:35:09,407 --> 00:35:12,277
How do you know that?

578
00:35:12,277 --> 00:35:13,511
I’ve been around, kid.

579
00:35:13,511 --> 00:35:16,581
- And i’ve been a square kid.
- No.

580
00:35:16,581 --> 00:35:18,216
Tell me more about them.

581
00:35:18,216 --> 00:35:19,718
Their faces
are lumpy and whiskered.

582
00:35:19,718 --> 00:35:22,854
Oh, wait, that’s me.

583
00:35:22,854 --> 00:35:24,422
The race
ruled this land once.

584
00:35:24,422 --> 00:35:26,257
They ruled this one acre
for about a week.

585
00:35:26,257 --> 00:35:27,325
Nobody knew.

586
00:35:27,325 --> 00:35:31,596
The race
of the ziox civilization.

587
00:35:31,596 --> 00:35:34,199
- Ziox?
- Wasn’t that a sandwich cookie?

588
00:35:34,199 --> 00:35:38,403
My dad wrote about them.

589
00:35:38,403 --> 00:35:40,739
Bto was such
a great band, man.

590
00:35:40,739 --> 00:35:43,441
Look.

591
00:35:43,441 --> 00:35:45,877
I’m about to puke, kid.
You might want to clear out.

592
00:35:45,877 --> 00:35:48,013
Look at the writing.

593
00:35:48,013 --> 00:35:49,414
It’s ancient.

594
00:35:49,414 --> 00:35:52,417
Old as the crumbs
in your moustache.

595
00:35:52,417 --> 00:35:55,220
Where does this lead to?

596
00:35:55,220 --> 00:35:57,689
Well, nobody knows
for sure...

597
00:35:57,689 --> 00:36:00,191
Except my dad, but um...

598
00:36:00,191 --> 00:36:01,960
I disappointed him.

599
00:36:01,960 --> 00:36:04,129
He was killed
seven years ago.

600
00:36:04,129 --> 00:36:06,431
And I want to know
why he died.

601
00:36:06,431 --> 00:36:08,800
This map is my only lead.

602
00:36:08,800 --> 00:36:11,202
Yeah, hang on. [Burps]

603
00:36:11,202 --> 00:36:12,570
Go to sleep, kid.

604
00:36:12,570 --> 00:36:14,072
I’m taking you home
in the morning.

605
00:36:14,072 --> 00:36:17,676
Oh, I think he’s taking him home
in the morning. Yeah, yeah.

606
00:36:17,676 --> 00:36:19,044
Yup.

607
00:36:22,247 --> 00:36:23,848
Rowsdower?

608
00:36:23,848 --> 00:36:25,917
[Laughing]

609
00:36:25,917 --> 00:36:26,951
Yeah?

610
00:36:26,951 --> 00:36:30,221
Why do I feel like
having haggis?

611
00:36:30,221 --> 00:36:32,624
- Have you always been a--
- hopeless drunk.

612
00:36:32,624 --> 00:36:35,527
Drifter?

613
00:36:35,527 --> 00:36:39,330
Rowsdower, could you
put out my head?

614
00:36:39,330 --> 00:36:40,932
No.

615
00:36:40,932 --> 00:36:42,033
Oh.

616
00:36:42,033 --> 00:36:43,535
Well, what were you before?

617
00:36:43,535 --> 00:36:48,073
Well, I used to give plasma.
You might know me from that.

618
00:36:48,073 --> 00:36:52,510
- I was a--
- a chippendales dancer.

619
00:36:52,510 --> 00:36:55,480
A businessman.

620
00:36:55,480 --> 00:36:56,915
What happened?

621
00:36:56,915 --> 00:37:00,018
Well, I switched to beating up
annoying kids with beer bottles.

622
00:37:07,058 --> 00:37:08,326
Go to sleep, kid.

623
00:37:08,326 --> 00:37:12,397
You’re harshing my buzz.

624
00:37:12,397 --> 00:37:16,601
Huh, now is this touching
or boring? I can’t...

625
00:37:16,601 --> 00:37:20,071
Really...

626
00:37:20,071 --> 00:37:21,906
Rowsdower.

627
00:37:25,610 --> 00:37:28,746
Now that is a darling
maxi skirt.

628
00:37:31,616 --> 00:37:36,121
[Yawns]
Rowsdower.

629
00:37:36,121 --> 00:37:39,324
Wow, I dreamt I was stuck
with a chunky backwoods loser

630
00:37:39,324 --> 00:37:42,393
named rowsdower-- aah!

631
00:37:42,393 --> 00:37:45,730
[Coughs] I think
my voice changed overnight.

632
00:37:48,766 --> 00:37:50,668
Good morning.

633
00:37:52,871 --> 00:37:56,508
So you gonna get us
out of here?

634
00:37:56,508 --> 00:37:57,575
I’ll get us out of here.

635
00:37:57,575 --> 00:38:01,146
Then we’ll stall
50 yards down the line.

636
00:38:01,146 --> 00:38:05,583
Why were you going to
turn me over to the cops?

637
00:38:05,583 --> 00:38:07,352
Because I like to keep
my nose clean.

638
00:38:07,352 --> 00:38:09,220
My body suffers
for it, but...

639
00:38:09,220 --> 00:38:11,656
Helping a runaway kid
can get me in big trouble.

640
00:38:11,656 --> 00:38:14,659
I’d love for you to meet
the people in my youth group.

641
00:38:17,762 --> 00:38:20,131
Rowsdower?

642
00:38:20,131 --> 00:38:22,433
Have you ever bathed?

643
00:38:22,433 --> 00:38:25,303
Will you help me find
what’s behind the map?

644
00:38:25,303 --> 00:38:28,873
Oh, I don’t go
map finding behinding.

645
00:38:28,873 --> 00:38:30,475
You should be in school.

646
00:38:30,475 --> 00:38:33,945
Not running around
hunting down lost civilizations.

647
00:38:33,945 --> 00:38:36,514
Besides, the map
could be a fake.

648
00:38:36,514 --> 00:38:38,283
A fantasy of your old man’s.

649
00:38:38,283 --> 00:38:40,585
Why do you think those men
were following us yesterday?

650
00:38:40,585 --> 00:38:42,687
Ah, they thought I was that guy
from due south.

651
00:38:42,687 --> 00:38:44,489
Don’t you see?

652
00:38:44,489 --> 00:38:46,124
They were after this.

653
00:38:46,124 --> 00:38:49,794
Rowsdower’s got one
of screendom’s best rear ends.

654
00:38:49,794 --> 00:38:52,764
Mm-hmm.

655
00:38:52,764 --> 00:38:55,166
You give me a hand now, kid.

656
00:38:55,166 --> 00:38:57,669
Rowsdower!

657
00:39:04,943 --> 00:39:07,812
Do you know how fast
you were going, rowsdower?

658
00:39:10,215 --> 00:39:14,619
Come on.

659
00:39:14,619 --> 00:39:16,287
Come on, baby.
Don’t let me down.

660
00:39:16,287 --> 00:39:18,756
I won’t, rowsdower.

661
00:39:18,756 --> 00:39:22,660
[Engine turns over]
Watch out, kid.

662
00:39:22,660 --> 00:39:27,065
Rowsdower-er-er-er.

663
00:39:27,065 --> 00:39:29,667
Damn.

664
00:39:29,667 --> 00:39:33,137
You’re going to drive
while I push at the front.

665
00:39:33,137 --> 00:39:34,505
Start out slow.

666
00:39:34,505 --> 00:39:36,674
When you get up some speed,
floor her. Got it?

667
00:39:36,674 --> 00:39:38,042
And i’d like
to thank dan aykroyd

668
00:39:38,042 --> 00:39:40,345
for doing that last line.

669
00:39:44,115 --> 00:39:47,886
Go!

670
00:39:47,886 --> 00:39:50,521
Fudge.

671
00:39:50,521 --> 00:39:53,258
Children and pregnant women
should not watch this scene.

672
00:39:53,258 --> 00:39:54,826
You know, in fact, no one
should really watch

673
00:39:54,826 --> 00:39:55,893
any of these scenes.

674
00:39:55,893 --> 00:39:57,328
- Yeah, you’re right.
- I agree.

675
00:40:00,832 --> 00:40:02,200
This is like
when our nursing home

676
00:40:02,200 --> 00:40:04,869
volunteer bus broke down.

677
00:40:04,869 --> 00:40:07,105
[Explosion]
Wow!

678
00:40:07,105 --> 00:40:09,874
Sounds like rowsdower’s heart
just exploded.

679
00:40:13,211 --> 00:40:15,380
[Heavy panting]

680
00:40:15,380 --> 00:40:17,282
I don’t think
that was a very good idea.

681
00:40:17,282 --> 00:40:18,917
Shut up.

682
00:40:18,917 --> 00:40:20,518
We’re in for a long walk.

683
00:40:20,518 --> 00:40:23,021
- We’re gonna walk?
- Well, it’s not my fault!

684
00:40:23,021 --> 00:40:26,724
You’re the one
that got us into this mess.

685
00:40:26,724 --> 00:40:28,726
You stay here
while I go get us some water.

686
00:40:28,726 --> 00:40:32,697
- I’ll go.
- Can you carry me?

687
00:40:32,697 --> 00:40:34,265
Canteen’s in the cab.

688
00:40:34,265 --> 00:40:37,235
AND THE CAB’S DOWN
AT COLUMBUS AND 77th.

689
00:40:43,574 --> 00:40:47,245
And if you find a package store,
get me some yukon jack.

690
00:40:54,185 --> 00:40:56,788
Thanks for the ride, mister.

691
00:40:59,023 --> 00:41:01,893
Well, I try to work out,
but it just gets hard.

692
00:41:07,932 --> 00:41:10,635
♪ Getting water
for rowsdower ♪

693
00:41:10,635 --> 00:41:13,471
♪ rowsdower wants me
to get water for him ♪

694
00:41:13,471 --> 00:41:16,240
[Sniffs]
Ew, nature smells.

695
00:41:16,240 --> 00:41:18,109
Mike, is there any way
I could hop into the movie

696
00:41:18,109 --> 00:41:19,410
and dump this kid’s books?

697
00:41:19,410 --> 00:41:21,713
Oh, I only wish.

698
00:41:21,713 --> 00:41:24,582
Somebody covered
their tomato plants.

699
00:41:29,754 --> 00:41:32,957
Let’s see what my cap’n crunch
treasure map says.

700
00:41:36,928 --> 00:41:39,097
[Growls]

701
00:41:42,066 --> 00:41:45,036
The three baguettes.

702
00:41:45,036 --> 00:41:48,072
[Grunts]

703
00:41:50,908 --> 00:41:54,545
♪ Rowsdower, rowsdower,
rowse-a-rowse-a-rowsedower ♪

704
00:41:54,545 --> 00:41:56,381
♪ bowse-a-bowse-a-bowesdower ♪

705
00:41:56,381 --> 00:41:58,182
♪ sabidi-sabidi-sowsdower ♪

706
00:41:58,182 --> 00:41:59,884
♪ bippity-boppity-bowsedower ♪

707
00:41:59,884 --> 00:42:02,520
♪ boppity-doppity-dower-rowse ♪

708
00:42:02,520 --> 00:42:04,122
♪ dower ♪

709
00:42:06,691 --> 00:42:09,694
Somebody’s breaking
shredded-wheat biscuits.

710
00:42:13,598 --> 00:42:16,000
Okay, I dropped the canteen,
and I got lost.

711
00:42:16,000 --> 00:42:17,702
Right on schedule.

712
00:42:17,702 --> 00:42:20,038
Ah, next I have to fall,
break my ankle,

713
00:42:20,038 --> 00:42:22,874
