and buried by a bear.

714
00:42:22,874 --> 00:42:25,576
[Howling]

715
00:42:30,648 --> 00:42:33,951
Take a left at the tree.
That helps!

716
00:42:35,686 --> 00:42:37,622
♪♪

717
00:42:43,928 --> 00:42:45,496
Bad news, losers.

718
00:42:45,496 --> 00:42:46,864
We won’t be in today

719
00:42:46,864 --> 00:42:49,934
because bobo ate a bad can
of canadian bacon,

720
00:42:49,934 --> 00:42:51,736
and he came down
with hockey hair,

721
00:42:51,736 --> 00:42:54,005
and now we’ve all got it.

722
00:42:54,005 --> 00:42:56,240
Lady? Lady.

723
00:42:56,240 --> 00:42:58,810
Can I watch power rangers?

724
00:43:00,578 --> 00:43:02,613
Well gee, pearl,
that’s too bad.

725
00:43:02,613 --> 00:43:04,449
I guess that means
it’s contagious.

726
00:43:04,449 --> 00:43:06,751
Oh, i’m sure you guys
will be fine.

727
00:43:06,751 --> 00:43:08,386
I mean, we live with the ape,

728
00:43:08,386 --> 00:43:11,022
so when he gets hockey hair,
we all get hockey hair.

729
00:43:11,022 --> 00:43:12,857
Don’t worry.

730
00:43:12,857 --> 00:43:16,627
The-- the doctor says
I have to have more whoppers

731
00:43:16,627 --> 00:43:19,530
and malted milk balls.

732
00:43:19,530 --> 00:43:22,133
Yes, yes, dear.

733
00:43:22,133 --> 00:43:26,003
Oh, for crying--
it’s an airborne virus. Sheesh.

734
00:43:26,003 --> 00:43:28,072
Mike, what’s your deal?
How come you don’t have it?

735
00:43:28,072 --> 00:43:32,376
Oh, I had it once already
from 1982 to 1992.

736
00:43:32,376 --> 00:43:34,378
Once you get it once,
you can’t get it again.

737
00:43:34,378 --> 00:43:35,613
Huh.

738
00:43:35,613 --> 00:43:39,417
Oh, no.
You guys got it too, huh?

739
00:43:39,417 --> 00:43:42,620
Well, the best thing is to
just let it run its course.

740
00:43:42,620 --> 00:43:45,056
Well, I think it’s great!

741
00:43:45,056 --> 00:43:47,325
I’ve never felt so masculine.

742
00:43:47,325 --> 00:43:49,594
I feel like guy lafleur.

743
00:43:49,594 --> 00:43:53,998
It’s time...
For my hourly ben and jerry’s.

744
00:43:55,933 --> 00:43:58,669
Huh, I have this intense
craving for zubaz.

745
00:43:58,669 --> 00:44:00,571
Yeah, you’re gonna get that.
[Alarm buzzes]

746
00:44:00,571 --> 00:44:03,508
- Oh, the movie’s playing.
- Oh, sherry!

747
00:44:14,085 --> 00:44:17,188
- Whoa, woozy.
- Sorry, you guys.

748
00:44:17,188 --> 00:44:18,222
Troy!

749
00:44:18,222 --> 00:44:21,993
It’s the canadian nick nolte.

750
00:44:21,993 --> 00:44:23,494
Troy, where are you?

751
00:44:23,494 --> 00:44:26,097
Mr. Aikman!

752
00:44:26,097 --> 00:44:27,598
Hey, mister,
have you seen rowsdower?

753
00:44:27,598 --> 00:44:28,733
Ah, hey.

754
00:44:28,733 --> 00:44:31,836
- Over here.
- What?

755
00:44:34,805 --> 00:44:36,274
Look what I found.

756
00:44:36,274 --> 00:44:39,243
What is it?

757
00:44:39,243 --> 00:44:41,245
It’s a tunnel.

758
00:44:41,245 --> 00:44:42,580
Yeah, right.

759
00:44:42,580 --> 00:44:45,683
That is a classic
rowsdowerism.

760
00:44:47,685 --> 00:44:50,221
A bug! Yuck!

761
00:44:58,729 --> 00:45:01,499
You’re going to throw me
down there, aren’t you?

762
00:45:05,236 --> 00:45:08,706
Yeah, not matter where he goes,
he finds a basement to dwell in.

763
00:45:11,909 --> 00:45:15,780
Excuse me.

764
00:45:15,780 --> 00:45:18,816
- Wow.
- These are really cheap sets.

765
00:45:20,685 --> 00:45:24,121
[Lighter flicks]

766
00:45:24,121 --> 00:45:26,257
This tunnel must have been dug
hundreds of years ago.

767
00:45:26,257 --> 00:45:27,625
I sensed that with my hair.

768
00:45:27,625 --> 00:45:29,260
My hair is an elaborate
network of nerves

769
00:45:29,260 --> 00:45:32,163
