Soon after, he threw me out.

958
00:57:20,704 --> 00:57:22,706
I-- ssh.

959
00:57:22,706 --> 00:57:25,642
Oh, it’s just a jackalope.

960
00:57:25,642 --> 00:57:28,645
Let’s get out of here.
This way.

961
00:57:28,645 --> 00:57:32,082
HMM, THAT’S A LITTLE TOO MUCH
DéCOLLETAGE FOR ME.

962
00:57:34,251 --> 00:57:37,321
Ah, any given weekend
in canada.

963
00:57:39,856 --> 00:57:43,226
Sides of his heart
are blowing out like old tires.

964
00:57:43,226 --> 00:57:47,464
[Tire popping sounds]

965
00:57:47,464 --> 00:57:49,599
[Panting]

966
00:57:53,570 --> 00:57:57,507
Rowsdower!

967
00:57:57,507 --> 00:58:00,243
[Panting]

968
00:58:00,243 --> 00:58:02,913
This is fun!

969
00:58:05,749 --> 00:58:09,353
They’ve stumbled upon
geddy lee’s birthplace.

970
00:58:09,353 --> 00:58:10,954
Okay.

971
00:58:10,954 --> 00:58:12,289
I guess we’ve had it.

972
00:58:12,289 --> 00:58:15,992
I probably only had about
three more months anyway.

973
00:58:15,992 --> 00:58:17,994
Not yet.

974
00:58:17,994 --> 00:58:20,530
It’s the wizard of id biathlon

975
00:58:24,568 --> 00:58:28,405
hey it looks like
their tin roof rusted.

976
00:58:32,075 --> 00:58:35,011
All right, abraham lincoln,
stop writing on that damn shovel

977
00:58:35,011 --> 00:58:37,013
